From 82c29602d1ed036bf832523bb46c98ff368b3fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hasan Mehdi <hasanthemehdi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:57:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bt: the bitrate follows the link, and each device keeps its
 own quality

In a pocket at the knee, resends of lost radio packets take the airtime the music
needed; the queue overflows and the stack throws music away. Packets thrown away now
step the SBC bitpool down (85/72/60% of the top, live, no reconfigure); a clear half
minute steps it back up, the wait doubling when going up brought the drops back.
High (dual channel) that drops falls back to standard until the next connection.

Sound quality is remembered per device: a 2013 Corolla played silence on high
(dual channel) while the earbuds took it. bt.log: link: behind / clear lines, and
packets dropped per stream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
